      "title": "The remainder and factor theorems",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "abbotsleigh2020-ext1-q3",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "The polynomial \\(P(x)=7x^3+9x^2-5cx\\) has factor \\(x+c\\), where \\(c\\ne0\\). Find \\(c\\).",
          "options": [
            "\\(2\\)",
            "\\(-2\\)",
            "\\(-1\\)",
            "\\(1\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "hint": "If (x+c) is a factor, substitute its zero, \\(x=-c\\), into (P(x)).",
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "has factor",
              "note": "The factor theorem says that \\(P(-c)=0\\)."
            }
          ],
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "The zero of the factor (x+c) is \\(x=-c\\). Apply the factor theorem.",
              "work": "\\(P(-c)=0\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Substitute (-c) into the polynomial and collect terms.",
              "work": "\\(7(-c)^3+9(-c)^2-5c(-c)= -7c^3+14c^2\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Use the condition (c\ne0), then solve.",
              "work": "\\(-7c^3+14c^2=7c^2(2-c)=0\\Rightarrow c=2\\)"
            }
          ],
          "solution": "\\(c=2\\)",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Abbotsleigh 2020 Trial Examination",
            "sourceFile": "/Users/andrewkim/Downloads/Abbotsleigh 2020.pdf",
            "school": "Abbotsleigh",
            "year": 2020
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "topicId": "y11e1-11E",
      "code": "11E",
      "title": "Consequences of the factor theorem",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "abbotsleigh2020-ext1-q5",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "stem": "The polynomial \\(P(x)=4x^3+8x^2-11x+3\\) has a double root \\(x=\\alpha\\). Find \\(\\alpha\\).",
          "options": [
            "\\(-3\\)",
            "\\(\\frac12\\)",
            "\\(-\\frac12\\)",
            "\\(3\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 1,
          "hint": "A double root is a repeated factor. Factor the cubic and identify which root occurs twice.",
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "has a double root",
              "note": "Look for a squared linear factor, not just any root."
            }
          ],
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Test a simple rational root. At \\(x=\\frac12\\), the polynomial is zero.",
              "work": "\\(P(1/2)=4(1/8)+8(1/4)-11(1/2)+3=0\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Factor the cubic. The squared factor identifies the repeated root.",
              "work": "\\(P(x)=(2x-1)^2(x+3)\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Set the repeated factor equal to zero.",
              "work": "\\(2x-1=0\\Rightarrow \\alpha=\\frac12\\)"
            }
          ],
          "solution": "\\(\\alpha=\\frac12\\)",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Abbotsleigh 2020 Trial Examination",
            "sourceFile": "/Users/andrewkim/Downloads/Abbotsleigh 2020.pdf",
            "school": "Abbotsleigh",
            "year": 2020
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "topicId": "y11e1-11F",
      "code": "11F",
      "title": "Sums and products of zeroes",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "ascham2020e1-q11b",
          "type": "mc",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "stem": "The polynomial \\(P(x)=x^3-4x^2+tx+10\\) has roots \\(\\alpha,-\\alpha,\\beta\\). What are the roots and the value of t?",
          "options": [
            "\\(\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac52},4;\\ t=\\frac52\\)",
            "\\(\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac52},-4;\\ t=-\\frac52\\)",
            "\\(\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac52},4;\\ t=-\\frac52\\)",
            "\\(\\pm\\sqrt5,4;\\ t=-5\\)"
          ],
          "answer": 2,
          "hint": "Use the sum of roots to find β. Then use the product of roots to find α² and the pairwise-product formula for the x coefficient.",
          "keyPoints": [
            {
              "text": "has roots \\(\\alpha,-\\alpha,\\beta\\)",
              "note": "The opposite pair cancels in the sum of roots."
            },
            {
              "text": "roots and the value of t",
              "note": "Use Vieta’s formulas for the sum, product, and sum of pairwise products."
            }
          ],
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "For a monic cubic x³−4x²+tx+10, the root sum is 4. Since α and −α cancel, β=4.",
              "work": "\\(\\alpha-\\alpha+\\beta=4\\Rightarrow\\beta=4\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "The product of the roots equals −10.",
              "work": "\\(\\alpha(-\\alpha)(4)=-10\\Rightarrow-4\\alpha^2=-10\\Rightarrow\\alpha^2=\\frac52\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "The x coefficient is the sum of pairwise products. The cross terms cancel.",
              "work": "\\(t=\\alpha(-\\alpha)+\\alpha\\beta-\\alpha\\beta=-\\alpha^2=-\\frac52\\)"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Combine the two values of α with β to list all three roots.",
              "work": "\\(\\boxed{\\alpha=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac52},\\quad\\beta=4,\\quad t=-\\frac52}\\)"
            }
          ],
          "solution": "Correct answer: \\(\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac52},4;\\ t=-\\frac52\\).",
          "timeLimit": 60,
          "xp": 1,
          "meta": {
            "source": "Ascham 2020 3U Trial",
            "examPaper": "Ascham 2020 3U Trial & Solutions"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
